_Garden_grille.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The railing of Summer Garden","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASummer_Garden_grille.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Krylov_monument_in_SPB_01.jpg/500px-Krylov_monument_in_SPB_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Krylov_monument_in_SPB_01.jpg/1280px-Krylov_monument_in_SPB_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Krylov_monument_in_SPB_01.jpg/500px-Krylov_monument_in_SPB_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The monument to Ivan Krylov in Summer Garden","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKrylov_monument_in_SPB_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Krylov_summer_garden.jpg/330px-Krylov_summer_garden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Krylov_summer_garden.jpg/330px-Krylov_summer_garden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The seated statue of the Russian 18-19 century fabulist, magazine publisher and librarian Ivan Krylov with pedestal showing the animal characters of his fables. The first Russia's monument to a private person. Sculptor Baron Peter Clodt von Jürgensburg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKrylov_summer_garden.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Letniy_Sad.jpg/500px-Letniy_Sad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Letniy_Sad.jpg/500px-Letniy_Sad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thum